From 857316b0d0d68cd9560bfd1405b2ae8d483a1559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:01:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: options shared by the backends of both
 interfaces

The options `execution_policy`, `device_stack_size`,
`data_transfer_policy` and `execution_space` are declared and read by
functions shared by the backends of the interfaces for material
properties and for behaviours (`MFront/GenericParallel/BackendOptions.hxx`),
instead of six copies of the same code. The Kokkos execution space, written
in the generated code, must now be a qualified C++ identifier.

The documentation explains why both interfaces are implemented
differently and why their statuses follow different conventions.
